  "id": "Compound::DB01403 - Gene::1132",
  "verbalization": "Methotrimeprazine appears to interact with Chrm4 through a shared pathway involving G-protein coupled receptors. The evidence suggests that Methotrimeprazine binds to Chrm2, which then participates in G-protein coupled receptor activity or muscarinic acetylcholine receptor activity, both of which are linked to Chrm4. This indicates a potential mechanism where Methotrimeprazine influences Chrm4 via a common intermediary, likely through modulation of acetylcholine receptor function. The overlapping roles of Chrm2 in different receptor activities highlight a possible convergence in the signaling pathways that Methotrimeprazine may engage. The consistent binding to Chrm2 and the subsequent participation in receptor activity pathways support a unified mechanism by which Methotrimeprazine may affect Chrm4, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
